    description: "react_component.py (~line 268) emits `references` edges whose src is\n\n    src_id = f\"typescript:{rel_path}:0-0:{comp_name}:jsx_usage\"\n\n-- a FABRICATED id: the linker's result carries only edges, no Symbol is minted for it, so the src matches no node and dangles. It also hardcodes `typescript` regardless of the file's language (sibling of WI-komum's hardcoded-language class).\n\nFound by the WI-latup derived_from sweep (verdict group 4). derived_from there is now `[target_sym.id]` (the only consumed record) with an `endpoints` declaration.\n\nFIX SHAPE: either anchor src on the enclosing component/function (`ctx.find_enclosing_symbol`) -- the edge then says \"this component renders that one\" -- or mint a real usage Symbol. The first is the one other linkers use. Verify with the dangling-endpoint check."  # 2ab3
